  {
   "id": "money",
   "short": "The money",
   "title": "The money and the politics",
   "dek": "Contracts, prize money, draft prices, and the rulebook split.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "facts",
     "items": [
      {
       "fact": "Pros earn from four places: UPA contracts (guaranteed salary), prize money, MLP team contracts, and equipment deals (paddle, ball, apparel). The UPA says 2026 shifts pay from salary toward prize money.",
       "source": "https://pickleball.com/news/upa-works-to-extend-pro-contracts-will-pay-out-millions-in-prize-money"
      },
      {
       "fact": "The UPA's plan: up to $31M in player earnings starting 2026: $11M guaranteed, $15M domestic prize money (PPA + MLP), $5M international.",
       "source": "https://pickleball.com/news/upa-works-to-extend-pro-contracts-will-pay-out-millions-in-prize-money"
      },
      {
       "fact": "In the 2026 MLP draft the St. Louis Shock paid $1.23 million for Anna Bright and the New Jersey 5s paid $800,000 for Jorja Johnson. A salary cap and floor are expected for 2027.",
       "source": "https://www.thedinkpickleball.com/the-new-jersey-fives-take-home-the-2026-mlp-championship/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "Anna Leigh Waters left Paddletek for a long-term Franklin deal in January 2026. Terms weren't disclosed; the $10M figure going around is podcast speculation.",
       "source": "https://pickleballrookie.com/the-biggest-paddle-deal-in-pickleball-history-contract-drama-rocks-the-pro-tour-and-mlp-heads-to-disney-world"
      },
      {
       "fact": "APP pro prize money: $1.5M across 2026, doubling to $3M in 2027 across 12 events.",
       "source": "https://www.theapp.global/news/app-tour-doubles-professional-prize-money-expands-2027-tour-schedule"
      },
      {
       "fact": "The 2026 US Open in Naples drew more than 500 pros for a purse of more than $160,000.",
       "source": "https://www.marconews.com/story/sports/2026/04/10/2026-us-open-pickleball-championships-gets-underway-in-east-naples/89561007007/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "UPA-A paddle certification costs a brand $10,000 a year plus $3,000 per paddle (valid 24 months), with paid rush options up to $7,500.",
       "source": "https://upaa.unitedpickleball.com/paddle-testing/2026-upa-a-certification/"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Who runs what",
     "type": "facts",
     "items": [
      {
       "fact": "MLP and the PPA Tour merged in 2024 under the United Pickleball Association (UPA), which runs both.",
       "source": "https://majorleaguepickleball.co/news/major-league-pickleball-announces-full-2026-may-august-season-schedule-event-tickets-now-on-sale-via-tixr-and-ticketmaster-2/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "In May 2024 the UPA replaced USA Pickleball as its governing body with its own UPA of America (UPA-A). USA Pickleball had been the only US governing body since 1984.",
       "source": "https://www.thedinkpickleball.com/upa-severs-ties-with-usa-pickleball/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "Two paddle rulebooks now: UPA-A certification (performance-tested: power and spin, after break-in) is required for PPA and MLP pro play since Sept 1, 2025. Amateur divisions just need the paddle on USA Pickleball's approved list.",
       "source": "https://upaa.unitedpickleball.com/paddle-testing/2026-upa-a-certification/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "UPA contracts are exclusive. In Dec 2025 it terminated three pros' contracts for playing unsanctioned events in Japan; they appealed.",
       "source": "https://www.thedinkpickleball.com/upa-terminates-contracts-of-ignatowich-fu-glozman-following-participation-in-unsanctioned-event/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "USA Pickleball still sanctions the US Open in Naples and runs its own National Championships, and partners with the APP on Golden Ticket qualifiers.",
       "source": "https://www.thedinkpickleball.com/dupr-is-now-the-official-ratings-partner-of-usa-pickleball/"
      },
      {
       "fact": "The senior pro league (50+) formerly called the National Pickleball League is now Champions Series Pickleball, licensed since March 2026 as the MLP Champions Series, with 16 teams.",
       "source": "https://majorleaguepickleball.co/news/major-league-pickleball-announces-partnership-with-pro-senior-pickleball-league-champions-series-pickleball-csp/"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
